# Both Dockerfiles build with `dockerContext: .` and do `COPY . .`, so this one root file
# covers them both.
#
# This is a correctness file, not hygiene. Without it the host's node_modules — installed on
# Windows, containing platform-specific binaries for sharp and the Prisma query engine — is
# copied over the Linux node_modules that the `deps` stage just installed, and the image runs
# on a corrupted dependency tree. It also stops apps/api/.env and apps/web/.env.local from
# being baked into an image layer, where they would survive in the image history.

node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

.git
.gitignore
.github
.husky
.vscode
.idea

.turbo
**/.turbo
**/dist
**/.next
**/out
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.eslintcache

# Secrets. The negations must come after the broad patterns to take effect.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

docs
*.md
!CLAUDE.md

Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
